'''Southeastern Kaftia''' is a large region of the continent of [[Kaftia]] on the planet [[Adonia]], encompassing the landmass east of the [[Southwestern Kaftia]] peninsula and extending from the [[Aethiopean Ocean]] in the west to the [[Kendriyan Ocean]] in the east. The region is home to 11 sovereign states and is one of the most geographically and culturally diverse regions on the continent. It is bounded by the [[Aethiopean Ocean]] to the west, the [[Mesogean Sea]] to the south, the [[Kendriyan Ocean]] to the east, and connects to [[Southwestern Kaftia]] in the west through [[Orma]] and to [[Illypnia]] in the northeast via the [[Triphylian Isthmus]].

The region is defined by the eastern extension of the [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]], which traverses the western portion of the region through [[Orma]], [[Ayorin]], and [[Enfolo]] before terminating at the [[Desket Escarpment]] on the [[Kendriyan Ocean]] coast. The northern portion of the region is dominated by the vast [[Central Kaftian Desert|Tanaruf n-Azref]], the homeland of the [[Imfezzan peoples]].

Southeastern Kaftia is the birthplace of the [[Qush civilization]], the earliest known civilization in Kaftia, which emerged in the river valleys of [[Jarin]] approximately 5,000 years ago. The region subsequently gave rise to numerous empires and trading states, and served as a crossroads connecting Kaftia to [[Illypnia]] via the [[Triphylian Isthmus]].

== Geography ==

=== The Great Kaftian Mountain Range ===
{{main|Great Kaftian Mountain Range}}
The '''[[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]]''' extends into Southeastern Kaftia from the southwest, forming the western spine of the region. The range enters the region through [[Orma]] and [[Ayorin]], where it forms the '''Eastern Divide''' along the border between the two countries, before continuing eastward through [[Enfolo]] and terminating at the [[Desket Escarpment]].

==== Eastern Divide ====
The Eastern Divide section averages 800–1,200 m in elevation and is characterised by montane forest on the northern slopes and drier open grassland on the southern slopes. The highest point in the Eastern Divide is '''[[Tulluu Wabbii]]''' (1,850 m), located along the Orma–Ayorin border. The name derives from Oromo, meaning "Mountain of the Gazelle."

The '''[[Gara Pass]]''' is the principal crossing point through the Eastern Divide, connecting the highlands of Orma with the lowlands of Ayorin. Historically used by trade caravans and migrating peoples, the pass remains an important transportation corridor.

==== Enfolo Plateau ====
{{main|Enfolo Plateau}}
The range reaches its greatest width in [[Enfolo]], where it forms a broad elevated plateau covering approximately 1,501,577 km². Rising 1,000–1,500 m in elevation, the plateau supports dense tropical jungle and receives the highest rainfall in the entire [[Great Kaftian Mountain Range]] system. The combination of elevation and equatorial moisture produces a {{W|cloud forest}} ecosystem unique in Kaftia.

The Enfolo Plateau serves as the principal watershed for Southeastern Kaftia's southern rivers. The [[Gash River|Gash]], [[Baraka River|Baraka]], [[Wori River|Wori]], [[Laga Gololcha]], and [[Laga Melka]] all originate on the plateau's southern slopes, draining toward the [[Mesogean Sea]].

==== Desket Escarpment ====
At the eastern terminus, in [[Desket]], the range forms the '''Desket Escarpment''' — a steep {{W|escarpment}} dropping 1,200–1,500 m to the [[Kendriyan Ocean]] coastal plain. The cliff faces are near-vertical in places, creating one of the most dramatic coastlines in Kaftia where the mountains meet the sea.

The coastal strip below the escarpment is 15–30 km wide and lies in a pronounced rain shadow, receiving significantly less precipitation than the plateau above. This arid coastal zone contrasts sharply with the humid cloud forests at the escarpment's summit.

=== Eastern Coast ===
The eastern coast of Southeastern Kaftia faces the [[Kendriyan Ocean]] and comprises the coastal nations of [[Desket]] and [[Nabia]]. This coastline is characterised by the dramatic Desket Escarpment in the north and more gentle coastal plains in the south near Nabia.

[[Nabia]], located between Desket and the [[Triphylian Isthmus]], features a more moderate coastal terrain with [[Lake Keren]] as its major inland water body. The country serves as a transitional zone between the arid Desket coast and the Mediterranean-influenced Triphylian region.

=== Northern Desert Region ===
{{main|Tamazgha}}
The northern portion of Southeastern Kaftia is dominated by the '''[[Central Kaftian Desert|Tanaruf n-Azref]]''' (Great Sand Sea), a vast expanse of {{W|erg (landform)|erg}} (sand dune fields) covering much of [[Tamazgha]]. This region is one of the most arid on [[Adonia]], receiving less than 100 mm of rainfall annually in most areas.

The desert landscape is punctuated by:
* '''Highland escarpments''' along the northern frontier, reaching elevations over 2,000 m
* '''Oasis belts''' supporting sedentary agricultural populations
* '''Volcanic highlands''' (''Adrar n-Tidawt'') in the southeast, featuring basalt formations and crater lakes
* '''Salt flats''' (''Tazruyt n-Isli''), remnants of ancient lakes and the lowest point in Southeastern Kaftia at -85 m below sea level

=== Sea of Hilal ===
{{main|Sea of Hilal}}
The '''[[Sea of Hilal]]''' is a large body of water in the eastern portion of the region, bounded by the Kaftian mainland to the west and the island of [[Hilal]] to the southeast. The sea connects to the open [[Kendriyan Ocean]] through two straits:

* '''[[Strait of Azref]]''': The northern strait, approximately 435 km wide at its narrowest point, separating Hilal from [[North Kaftia]].
* '''[[Strait of Guzo]]''': The southern strait, approximately 176 km wide at its narrowest point, separating Hilal from the [[Desket]]–[[Nabia]] coast. The name derives from Amharic ''guzo'', meaning "passage" or "journey."

[[Hilal]] is the only major island in the sea, with a distinctive curved shape resembling an arrowhead pointing eastward toward the Kendriyan Ocean.

=== Southern Coast ===
The southern coast of Southeastern Kaftia faces the [[Mesogean Sea]] and comprises a Mediterranean-climate coastal strip backed by hills and highlands. The coast is characterised by natural harbours, river mouths, and sporadic hills. The [[Triphylian Isthmus]] at the eastern end of the coast forms a narrow land bridge connecting Kaftia to [[Illypnia]] and the nation of [[Lagash]].

==== Triphylian Isthmus ====
{{main|Triphylian Isthmus}}
The '''[[Triphylian Isthmus]]''' is a narrow strip of land connecting the Kaftian continent to [[Illypnia]] and the nation of [[Lagash]]. At its narrowest point, the isthmus measures approximately 120 km across. The terrain is generally flat to gently hilly, making it a natural corridor for trade and migration between the two continents.

The '''[[Triphylian Canal]]''' crosses the isthmus, providing a navigable waterway for maritime traffic between the [[Mesogean Sea]] and the [[Kendriyan Ocean]].

=== Western Delta Region ===
The western coast of Southeastern Kaftia, along the [[Aethiopean Ocean]], is dominated by the [[Amara Delta]] in [[Ayorin]] — one of the largest river deltas on the continent.

==== Amara Delta ====
{{main|Amara Delta}}
The '''[[Amara Delta]]''' covers approximately 149,468 km², representing 25.1% of [[Ayorin]]'s total land area. It is formed by 15 major rivers draining from the highlands into the [[Bight of Ayorin]]. The delta supports dense agricultural populations and extensive wetland ecosystems, including mangrove forests and diverse bird populations.

The [[Bight of Ayorin]] is a major coastal feature indenting the shoreline of Ayorin and [[Tamazgha]].

== Hydrography ==

=== Rivers ===
Southeastern Kaftia has a mixed drainage system, with rivers flowing into three different bodies of water: the [[Aethiopean Ocean]], [[Mesogean Sea]], and [[Kendriyan Ocean]]. The [[Enfolo Plateau]] serves as the principal watershed divide for the southern rivers.

